WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.602 --> 00:00:03.435
(trumpet playing)

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:06.860
- [Narrator] Once upon a
time on the island of Sicily,

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:10.263
there was a race that ran
right through your village.

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:13.400
It was glorious.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:14.550
It was beautiful.

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:18.343
It was clearly planned before
safety was a consideration.

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:27.370
The Targa Florio was founded in Sicily

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:31.680
by a speed loving fellow
named Vincenzo Florio in 1906.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:34.433
And it enthralled the racing
world for decades to come.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.520
But this was no ordinary race.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:41.380
It took place in the
mountains outside of Palermo.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:45.920
Racers encountered bandits,
wolves, 500-plus hairpin turns

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.883
on roads that hadn't changed
since togas were in fashion.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.650
The course went straight
through towns and villages

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.090
with no barricades or warnings.

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:58.340
The first year a driver
named Alessandro Cagno won.

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:00.580
It took him nine hours
and his average speed

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:01.883
was 30 miles an hour.

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:06.450
The Targa Florio ran for 71 years.

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:09.830
Titans of the car world like
Mario Andretti competed,

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:11.520
but a growing realization that the race

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.920
was crazy dangerous led to
it being shut down in 1977.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:17.550
It was the longest running car race

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.290
in the world at the time.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:23.470
Today, the grandstand
outside Palermo sits empty,

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:26.060
but evidence of the race is everywhere,

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:29.200
peaking out in the beautiful landscape.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.070
The Targa Florio became synonymous

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:33.350
with a long and grueling race.

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:35.130
In the years after its end,

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:37.850
tribute Targas have popped
up across the world,

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:41.403
but true racing enthusiasts
know it all began here.

